text = "FEATURE | The Mind Recorded
Neurological Blackboxes and the end of forgetting
By Dr. Varrin Essel
Published in The Solarian Observer

It began as an innovation in accident forensics.
A neural implant at the base of the skull, capable of tethering to nearby devices and drawing their feeds into a central chip.
These devices include but are no limited to: cameras, terminals, and even drones.
The result: a seamless record of the host's life from every available angle.

At first, its promise was undeniable. Collisions, industrial disasters, military engagements, all could be reconstructed with precision. No longer was the truth hidden in the chaos of events. 
Now, the Neurological Blackbox is compulsory. By mandate of the Coalition, every Citizen above the age of 21 Sol Years must undergo the procedure to have one implanted.
Officials insist the benefits are overwhelming. Perfect evidence, flawless accountability, and clarity in disputes.
\"Your life is your testimony,\" declared one Government spokesperson.
But many find no comfort in this certainty.
Where once a mistake could be forgotten, a word could fade, or a private moment would remain private, now all is preserved.

One unsettling truth: we may not simply use technology anymore.
We have become its content.
"
label_settings = ExtResource("20_q0khx")
autowrap_mode = 3

