text = "ListenClosely.wav

*The following is a transcript of the audio recording*

This is Dr George Burklee of the Galactic Astronomy Administration. The supernova event taking 
place within the VX-66458 system has resulted in a nebula that is slowly spreading across 
Solarian Space. 
This nebula is emitting a previously unknown type of radiation. Initial analysis indicates that 
exposure to this radiation causes severe neurological disturbances. Starting with radiation 
sickness then leading to memory loss, paranoia, insanity, increased aggression and finishing with 
complete loss of cognitive functions and humanity.

Any individuals showing these symptoms must be isolated and transported to the nearest GAA safe
zone for treatement.

This new type of radiation cannot seem to penetrate the metal alloys used in ships, stations and 
EVA suits. This means anyone who isn’t inside a ship or station or wearing an EVA suit is at risk of 
exposure, even on inhabited worlds. Scans on a nearby planet inidicate that the radiation can
affect the very air we breathe.

The nebula’s advance is faster than predicted. We believe… it shimmers… it’s beautiful… like…
No! No. Must stay focused.

The nebula is affecting the Interstellar Communications Network. We’ve lost contact with all 
outposts inside VX-66458 and the surrounding systems. Only shortwave radio seems to be unaffected.
If you have managed to receive this message, I urge you to stay inside your vessel for the sake of 
humanity… Do not listen to… the whispers… it’s… calling… I can hear it. It knows my name…
NO! Must… Stay… Focused…

But… Their faces… my colleagues… they were my friends…

AHHHHHH-…
"
label_settings = ExtResource("20_q0khx")

