text = "OPINION | The Numbers Behind the Stars
Are we living in a simulation?
By Dr. Ellian Vex
Published in The Solarian Observer

It begins as many things do, with a number.
Not one that changes markets or guides spacecrafts, but one that always
seems to appear.
Citizens across different systems, cultures, and professions have quietly
reported recurring numbers. For example: 1123, 3344, 512, 907.
These numbers are seen everywhere from starship diagnostic codes, 
personal ID numbers, planetary soil analyses, and even in
digitized genetic helix sequences.

A growing theory among philosophers suggests that such reptitions may not be
random at all. But instead the echoes of computational processes.
Their argument? That existance and the universe itself may be a simulation
of immense complexity and these numbers are the residue of virtual 
scaffolding, bleeding into observable space.

We may never be able to prove such a theory true or not, but new questions
open up:

If our universe is code,
who wrote it?

and, for what purpose?"
label_settings = ExtResource("20_q0khx")

