text = "FEATURE | Life Beyond Scale
The possibility of life beyond comprehension
By Dr. Halena Myrr
Published in The Solarian Observer

We spend much of our time searching for life we can understand.
Biological signatures, heat patterns or transmissions.
But what if the greatest threat to our continued existence does not seek us
out, does not communicate or may not even know we exist?

Recent gravitational anomalies near the outskirts of the VX-00907 system and 
the VX-66458 system have led some in the scientific community to revisit an 
old but unsettled hypothesis. The universe may be home to entities so 
vast, so fundamentally different in structure and perception, that our 
existence registers to them no more than bacteria does to us.

Such macrocosmic lifeforms, if they exist, would not be bound to the scale 
of flesh and matter, but prehaps to gravity wells, stellar currents or even
dark matter flows. They would not invade or attack.
They would simply move and in doing so, perhaps rupture the fabric of space,
extinguish stars, or collapse civilizations without intent, without malice
and without ever knowing they were there.

The unsettling truth: we may not be actors on the galactic stage, 
but fungal growth on its scaffolding.

And if we are crushed beneath such a being, it wouldn't be war.
It would be indifference."
label_settings = ExtResource("20_q0khx")

